<workflow>
  <name>set-password-encoder</name>
  <name_sync_with_filename>Y</name_sync_with_filename>
  <description/>
  <extended_description/>
  <created_user>-</created_user>
  <modified_user>-</modified_user>
  <created_date>2026/10/07 10:00:00.000</created_date>
  <modified_date>2026/10/07 10:00:00.000</modified_date>
  <created_hop_version/>
  <modified_hop_version/>
  <workflow_version/>
  <parameters/>
  <actions>
    <action>
      <repeat>N</repeat>
      <schedulerType>0</schedulerType>
      <intervalSeconds>0</intervalSeconds>
      <intervalMinutes>60</intervalMinutes>
      <DayOfMonth>1</DayOfMonth>
      <weekDay>1</weekDay>
      <minutes>0</minutes>
      <hour>12</hour>
      <doNotWaitOnFirstExecution>N</doNotWaitOnFirstExecution>
      <name>Start</name>
      <description/>
      <type>SPECIAL</type>
      <attributes/>
      <xloc>80</xloc>
      <yloc>256</yloc>
      <parallel>N</parallel>
      <attributes_hac/>
    </action>
    <action>
      <encoder_plugin_id>Hop</encoder_plugin_id>
      <key_variable/>
      <key_file/>
      <name>Set Hop encoder</name>
      <description/>
      <type>SET_PASSWORD_ENCODER</type>
      <attributes/>
      <xloc>272</xloc>
      <yloc>256</yloc>
      <parallel>N</parallel>
      <attributes_hac/>
    </action>
    <action>
      <loglevel>Basic</loglevel>
      <logsubject/>
      <logmessage>Passwords are now encoded with the default Hop encoder.</logmessage>
      <name>Done</name>
      <description/>
      <type>WRITE_TO_LOG</type>
      <attributes/>
      <xloc>464</xloc>
      <yloc>256</yloc>
      <parallel>N</parallel>
      <attributes_hac/>
    </action>
  </actions>
  <hops>
    <hop>
      <from>Start</from>
      <to>Set Hop encoder</to>
      <evaluation>Y</evaluation>
      <unconditional>Y</unconditional>
      <enabled>Y</enabled>
    </hop>
    <hop>
      <from>Set Hop encoder</from>
      <to>Done</to>
      <evaluation>Y</evaluation>
      <unconditional>N</unconditional>
      <enabled>Y</enabled>
    </hop>
  </hops>
  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>The Set password encoder action changes the encoder Hop uses to encrypt and decrypt passwords (for example in database connections) for the rest of the process.
Use it when a workflow has to read metadata that was encrypted with a different encoder, for example the AES2 encoder with the key in the HOP_AES_ENCODER_KEY variable.

This sample sets the default Hop encoder, which needs no key. Choose AES or AES2 and a key variable or key file to use one of the AES encoders.
Note that the encoder is changed for the whole Hop process: when you run this in Hop Gui, it is used until you restart.</note>
      <markdown>N</markdown>
      <notetype>GENERAL</notetype>
      <fontname>Segoe UI</fontname>
      <fontsize>11</fontsize>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
      <fontitalic>N</fontitalic>
      <fontcolorred>14</fontcolorred>
      <fontcolorgreen>58</fontcolorgreen>
      <fontcolorblue>90</fontcolorblue>
      <backgroundcolorred>201</backgroundcolorred>
      <backgroundcolorgreen>232</backgroundcolorgreen>
      <backgroundcolorblue>251</backgroundcolorblue>
      <bordercolorred>14</bordercolorred>
      <bordercolorgreen>58</bordercolorgreen>
      <bordercolorblue>90</bordercolorblue>
      <xloc>80</xloc>
      <yloc>32</yloc>
      <width>640</width>
      <height>192</height>
    </notepad>
  </notepads>
  <attributes/>
</workflow>
